h \loch \af6 \hich \af6 \dbch \af6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 {\listtext \pard \plain \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af6 \hich \af6 \dbch \af6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 \f1 D.\tab }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 They will still face the difficult choice between career and children.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s211 \qj \fi-1040 \li1040 \ri0 \sb0 \lisb0 \sa0 \lisa0 \sl-360 \slmult0 \nowidctlpar \keep1 \keepn1 \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin1040 \rin0 \cbpat16 \tql \tx3235 \tql \tx7622 \itap0 \outlinelevel5 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \b1 \fs36 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af5 \hich \af5 \dbch \af6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs93 \b0 \fs28 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af1 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 Passage Two}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs93 \b0 \fs28 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af1 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \sl360 \slmult1 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af6 \hich \af6 \dbch \af6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \b1 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 Questions 61 to 65 are based on the following passage.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \b1 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \fi360 \cufi200 \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \sl360 \slmult1 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af6 \hich \af6 \dbch \af6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 Some of the world\uc1 \u8217 ?s most significant problems never hit headlines. One example comes from agriculture. Food riots and hunger make news. But the trend lying behind these matters is rarely talked about. This is the decline in the growth in yields of some of the world\uc1 \u8217 ?s major crops. A new study by the University of Minnesota and McGill University in Montreal looks at where, and how far, this decline is occurring.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \fi360 \cufi200 \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \sl360 \slmult1 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af6 \hich \af6 \dbch \af6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 The authors take a vast number of data points for the four most important crops :rice, wheat, com and soyabeans }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1028 \langnp1028 \langfe1028 \langfenp1028 \alang1025 \cf1 (}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af0 \hich \af0 \dbch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf1 \'a4j\'a8\'a7}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf1 )}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 .They find that on between }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1028 \langnp1028 \langfe1028 \langfenp1028 \alang1025 \cf1 24% }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 and }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1028 \langnp1028 \langfe1028 \langfenp1028 \alang1025 \cf1 39% }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 of all harvested areas, the improvement in yields that took place before the 1980s slowed down in the 1990s and 2000s.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \fi360 \cufi200 \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \sl360 \slmult1 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af6 \hich \af6 \dbch \af6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 There are two worrying features of the slowdown. One is that it has been particularly sharp in the world\uc1 \u8217 ?s most}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 \tab }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 (}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af0 \hich \af0 \dbch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf1 \'a4H\'a4f\'a6h\'aa\'ba}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af0 \hich \af0 \dbch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 \'a1^}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 countries, India and China. Their ability to feed themselves has been an important source of relative stability both within the countries and on world food markets. That self-sufficiency cannot be taken for granted if yields continue to slow down or reverse.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \fi360 \cufi200 \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \sl360 \slmult1 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af6 \hich \af6 \dbch \af6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 Second, yield growth has been lower in wheat and rice than in com and soyabeans. This is problematic because wheat and rice are more important as foods, accounting for around half of all calories consumed. Com and soyabeans are more important as feed grains. The authors note that \uc1 \u8220 ?we have preferentially focused our crop improvement efforts on feeding animals and cars rather than on crops that feed people and are the basis of food security in much of the world. \uc1 \u8221 ?,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \fi360 \cufi200 \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \sl360 \slmult1 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af6 \hich \af6 \dbch \af6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 The report qualifies the more optimistic findings of another new paper which suggests that the world will not have to dig up a lot more land for farming in order to feed 9 billion people in 2050, as the Food and Agriculture Organisation has argued.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \fi360 \cufi200 \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \sl360 \slmult1 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \loch \af6 \hich \af6 \dbch \af6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 \alang1025 \cf1 Instead, it says, thanks to slowing population growth, land currently ploughed up for crops might be able to revert }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs18 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \lang1028 \langnp1028 \langfe1028 